  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: The current best configuration is rna_only + scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool (0.650). Strikingly, adding resnet50 image in multimodal mode actually *hurts* performance (config_030: 0.632 vs config_005: 0.650). However, resnet50 is a weak encoder (image_only accuracy is only 0.208), so it is unclear whether the image modality is fundamentally unhelpful or whether a stronger encoder would provide complementary signal. 2) What this tests: config_036 is a clean single-variable change from config_030 (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), holding model_setting=multimodal, profile=multiprofile, rna_encoder=scvi_n200, aggregation=avgpool, and fusion=concat constant. It directly asks whether a much stronger visual encoder can make the image modality additive with the best RNA encoder. 3) Why best next experiment: Under a limited budget, resolving whether image has any value with scvi_n200 is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question. A positive result opens the multimodal+ViT-L direction for further optimization; a negative result lets us confidently discard the image modality and focus remaining experiments on RNA encoder/aggregation improvements. No other single experiment reduces as much decision-relevant uncertainty."
}

